# Kenneth Nnorom

Network Security Engineer based in Lagos, Nigeria — building and breaking networks across enterprise IT and OT/converged environments.

## What I work on
- **Enterprise & Data Centre Networking** — MPLS WANs, VXLAN/EVPN fabrics, Cumulus Linux deployments across field sites and head office infrastructure
- **Network Security & Assessment** — Active Directory hardening, wireless and WAN exposure analysis, vulnerable-AD lab work (pfSense/Snort, Wazuh, Kali Purple)
- **Automation & Visibility** — Python tooling for network diagnostics (L2/L3 route classification via traceroute, ARP, HSRP/VRRP MAC patterns) and monitoring platforms

## Featured project
**[LNMP (Linux Network Monitoring Platform)](#)** — A FastAPI/TimescaleDB/Vue monitoring application, built as both a production tool and a structured Python-learning project (asyncio, dataclasses, state machines).

## Background
Electrical & Computer Engineering roots, now anchored in network engineering and cybersecurity. I write about breach analysis, lab builds, and infrastructure design — usually with a bias toward empirical over theoretical.

